  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="HH2FB9527C1D4BB25D79F1C0C76F5BC95D" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;American Transmission Systems, Incorporated (ATSI) has authorization from the Public Utilities Commission of Ohio (PUCO) to incur short-term debt of up to $500 million through bank facilities and FirstEnergy's regulated money pool. ATSI has the ability to borrow from its regulated affiliates and FirstEnergy Corp. (FE) to meet its short-term working capital requirements. FirstEnergy Service Company administers this money pool and tracks surplus funds of FE and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;the respective regulated subsidiary, as well as proceeds available from bank borrowings. Companies receiving a loan under the money pool agreements must repay the principal amount of the loan, together with accrued interest, within 364 days of borrowing the funds. The rate of interest is the same for each company receiving a loan from their respective pool and is based on the average cost of funds available through the pool. The average interest rate for borrowings for the first &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; months of 2026 was &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% per annum. &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;In April, 2026 ATSI issued $175 million of 5.19% senior unsecured notes due in 2033 and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; redeemed $75 million of 4.00% senior unsecured notes that became due. &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;
	&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
